@startuml
title `lower_equation` (macros/src/gen/runtime/dovetail_report.rs:1472) - why 3 equations become 4 rules

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
  DiamondBorderColor #1F2937
  DiamondFontColor #111827
  DiamondBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
  BackgroundColor<<equation>> #FEF3C7
  BackgroundColor<<failure>> #FEE2E2
  BackgroundColor<<engine>> #EDE9FE
  BackgroundColor<<inert>> #E5E7EB
  BackgroundColor<<result>> #DCFCE7
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #92400E
  BackgroundColor #FEF9C3
  FontColor #111827
}

start
:one `Equation` from `equations { }`
<latex>\mathit{lhs} \;=\; \mathit{rhs}</latex>; <<equation>>

if (every premise satisfies `premise_supported`? (:1479)) then (no)
  :record "equation has side conditions" in `unsupported`
  the language FAILS CLOSED - nothing is emitted; <<failure>>
  stop
else (yes - Monoid declares no premises at all)
endif

partition "FORWARD direction (:1484-1502)" {
  if (`eq.left.is_just_variable()`? (ast/src/pattern.rs:282)) then (yes)
    :emit nothing, SILENTLY - a bare-variable LHS
    would match every e-class in the graph; <<inert>>
  else (no)
    :`RewriteRule { lhs, rhs }`
    label `Monoid::equation::NAME::forward`; <<engine>>
  endif
}

partition "REVERSE direction (:1504-1524)" {
  if (`eq.right.is_just_variable()`?) then (yes)
    :emit nothing, SILENTLY; <<inert>>
  else (no)
    :`RewriteRule { lhs: rhs, rhs: lhs }`
    label `Monoid::equation::NAME::reverse`; <<engine>>
  endif
}

:the emitted rules join `__DOVETAIL_COMPILED_RULES`
(a `OnceLock`, compiled once per process); <<result>>
stop

note right
  APPLIED TO MONOID

  Assoc   lhs <latex>(X \cdot Y) \cdot Z</latex>  not a bare var  -> FORWARD
          rhs <latex>X \cdot (Y \cdot Z)</latex>  not a bare var  -> REVERSE
  UnitL   lhs <latex>e \cdot X</latex>            not a bare var  -> FORWARD
          rhs <latex>X</latex>                    IS a bare var   -> DROPPED
  UnitR   lhs <latex>X \cdot e</latex>            not a bare var  -> FORWARD
          rhs <latex>X</latex>                    IS a bare var   -> DROPPED

  3 equations  ->  4 rules, not 6. Verified in
  `target/generated/monoid/dovetail_report.rs:158-194`.
end note

note left
  Why dropping the unit REVERSE does not
  lose the quotient: a rule fires through
  `apply_structural_matches`
  (dovetail/src/rules.rs:804-807) as
  `self.merge(root, rhs_id)` - an UNDIRECTED
  union. One direction already identifies
  the two e-classes.

  Keeping <latex>X \rightsquigarrow e \cdot X</latex> would instead
  manufacture <latex>e \cdot X,\; e \cdot (e \cdot X),\; \ldots</latex>
  without bound and exhaust the node budget.
end note

@enduml
